tively. I'm glad I caught that detail to make sure I'm being helpful!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Thanks — that makes a **musculoskeletal lower back source** a bit more plausible, but with your kidney history it still does **not fully exclude a renal cause**, especially since the symptoms have been progressing.\n\nTo narrow it safely, please answer the **remaining key questions**:\n1. Does the pain **stay in one spot** or **radiate** to the side, abdomen, groin, or leg?\n2. Have you noticed **blood in the urine**, darker urine, burning, frequency, or reduced urine output?\n3. Any **fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, loss of appetite, or weight loss**?\n4. Are you still taking **sunitinib**, and when did the fatigue start relative to that treatment?\n5. Have you had any **recent CT/ultrasound, oncology follow-up, creatinine/eGFR, or hemoglobin** results after March 10?\n6. On a **0–10 scale**, how severe is the pain, and is it **constant or intermittent**?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_02bc3a321a4aa4d20169b984da3be081918e0647e3a4c08cd1\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":23816,"output":244,"cacheRead":11904,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":35964,"cost":{"input":0.05954,"output":0.00366,"cacheRead":0.002976,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.06617600000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773765846466}}
